  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: Sudden, severe left-sided headache that began ~4 hours ago.\n• Symptom details:\n  – Onset: Abrupt this morning, first episode of this kind.\n  – Location: Left side of head, sometimes described ‘behind the eye.’\n  – Severity: 6/10 (kidney-stone pain =10/10 reference).\n  – Associated features: Blurred vision with zig-zag lines (visual aura), dizziness, photophobia (can’t look at screens), nausea and 2 episodes of vomiting, feels worse when moving the head, prefers lying still.\n  – Aggravating/alleviating: Movement worsens; paracetamol taken 3 h ago gave no relief.\n• Past medical history: Kidney stones; no prior migraines.\n• Medications: None.  Paracetamol tried today.\n• Allergies: Denies known drug allergies.\n• Family history: Mother – migraines and hypothyroidism.\n• Social / obstetric: Pregnancy unlikely (patient statement). No other social history given.\n• Vital signs / physical exam: Tele-visit; no vitals supplied. Patient reports no focal weakness, normal gait.\n• Labs / imaging: None performed or mentioned.",
